837 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 658 0 R
/T (This report offers a consolidated, independent assessment of basic and secondary education in Bauchi State, Nigeria. It brings together household-survey evidence, national learning assessments, administrative school statistics, education financing records, programme documentation and comparative research to examine whether schooling is translating into learning, completion and equitable opportunity. The findings and policy options are intended for state institutions, legislators, education practitioners, researchers, development partners and the public.)
/E (This report offers a consolidated, independent assessment of basic and secondary education in Bauchi State, Nigeria. It brings together household-survey evidence, national learning assessments, administrative school statistics, education financing records, programme documentation and comparative research to examine whether schooling is translating into learning, completion and equitable opportunity. The findings and policy options are intended for state institutions, legislators, education practitioners, researchers, development partners and the public.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
838 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 658 0 R
/T (The central analytical lens is an education-delivery chain: participation, regular attendance, adequate teaching conditions, effective instruction, measured learning, educational progression and sustained institutional performance. The report examines how constraints and accountability failures at any stage may prevent increased investment or enrolment from producing better educational outcomes.)
/E (The central analytical lens is an education-delivery chain: participation, regular attendance, adequate teaching conditions, effective instruction, measured learning, educational progression and sustained institutional performance. The report examines how constraints and accountability failures at any stage may prevent increased investment or enrolment from producing better educational outcomes.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
