/T (Statewide averages can also conceal differences between metropolitan Bauchi, smaller rural settlements, remote communities and Islamic learning centres, as well as the experiences of children in economically mobile households. A child may face several barriers at once, including a long or unsafe journey to school, a teacher shortage, unusable toilets and pressure to work. The available administrative ratios can guide the selection of sites for fieldwork. Establishing where these barriers overlap requires school locations, settlement data, seasonal travel-time estimates, learner ages and household verification that protects privacy.)
