/T (A five-category participation system is analytically preferable to one aggregate headline. Children may be regular formal-school attendees; irregular formal-school attendees; participants in integrated recognised non-formal programmes; learners in unrecognised educational settings; or children with no sustained educational participation. Each category requires a different response and a documented method for identifying movement between categories. For transition analysis, school and provider data should record age, grade or learning level, prior status, attendance, completion, movement to secondary and verified learning outcomes, with privacy protections.)
/E (A five-category participation system is analytically preferable to one aggregate headline. Children may be regular formal-school attendees; irregular formal-school attendees; participants in integrated recognised non-formal programmes; learners in unrecognised educational settings; or children with no sustained educational participation. Each category requires a different response and a documented method for identifying movement between categories. For transition analysis, school and provider data should record age, grade or learning level, prior status, attendance, completion, movement to secondary and verified learning outcomes, with privacy protections.)
/Pg 24 0 R
