/E (The basic access problem becomes intelligible when participation is separated into five operational categories: children regularly attending recognised formal schools; formally enrolled children with irregular or seasonal attendance; children in integrated or recognised non-formal and Islamic education settings; children attending learning environments outside the official school registry; and children with no sustained educational participation. Each group encounters different barriers and needs a different policy response. [E03, E20])
