/P 671 0 R
/T (For the first group, priorities are retention, grade progression and learning quality. The second requires attendance case management and an investigation of costs, distance, mobility and child work. The third needs appropriate learning standards and viable transitions. The fourth needs safeguarding, community engagement and a measured recognition or equivalency pathway rather than automatic classification as learning failure. The fifth may require outreach, alternative provision, social support and safe access to schools. A single headline outof-school count cannot deliver those choices.)
/E (For the first group, priorities are retention, grade progression and learning quality. The second requires attendance case management and an investigation of costs, distance, mobility and child work. The third needs appropriate learning standards and viable transitions. The fourth needs safeguarding, community engagement and a measured recognition or equivalency pathway rather than automatic classification as learning failure. The fifth may require outreach, alternative provision, social support and safe access to schools. A single headline outof-school count cannot deliver those choices.)
