/T (The policy mechanism is not simply the construction of more pre-primary classrooms. Quality early childhood learning requires play-based materials, language-responsive instruction, child protection, nutrition and ageappropriate teaching, as well as a financially credible transition to the primary grades. Without these inputs, expanding nominal places can produce low-quality services that are difficult to sustain. Any early-years option for Bauchi should therefore be evaluated against qualified-staff availability, parent demand, facility suitability, proximity, unit cost and measurable school readiness.)
/E (The policy mechanism is not simply the construction of more pre-primary classrooms. Quality early childhood learning requires play-based materials, language-responsive instruction, child protection, nutrition and ageappropriate teaching, as well as a financially credible transition to the primary grades. Without these inputs, expanding nominal places can produce low-quality services that are difficult to sustain. Any early-years option for Bauchi should therefore be evaluated against qualified-staff availability, parent demand, facility suitability, proximity, unit cost and measurable school readiness.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
