/T (An education system does not produce learning merely by listing schools and classrooms. The relevant service question is whether a child can attend a safe, accessible learning environment in which qualified teaching occurs for the expected duration. That requires usable rooms, seating, learning materials, reliable water, functioning sanitation, hygiene supplies, inclusion supports, protective routines and an identified maintenance responsibility. The federal 2024/25 census reported 206.7 learners per toilet in Bauchi, considerably above the published national ratio of 65.9; this is a signal to inspect actual services, not a verified measurement of usable cubicles or accessibility. [E01])
/E (An education system does not produce learning merely by listing schools and classrooms. The relevant service question is whether a child can attend a safe, accessible learning environment in which qualified teaching occurs for the expected duration. That requires usable rooms, seating, learning materials, reliable water, functioning sanitation, hygiene supplies, inclusion supports, protective routines and an identified maintenance responsibility. The federal 2024/25 census reported 206.7 learners per toilet in Bauchi, considerably above the published national ratio of 65.9; this is a signal to inspect actual services, not a verified measurement of usable cubicles or accessibility. [E01])
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 681 0 R
/T (The denominator problem is more serious than it first appears. Federal portal counts for Bauchi record 1,932,456 learners and 21,227 classrooms, which yield approximately 91 learners per classroom if simply divided. The same portal displays a learner-to-classroom ratio of 66.6. Different school levels, definitions, ownership filters or room types may explain the mismatch; no alternative ratio should be substituted until the calculation rule and data extract are obtained. The fact that a simple arithmetic cross-check does not match is a legitimate request for metadata, not evidence that the underlying system is fraudulent. [E01])
/E (The denominator problem is more serious than it first appears. Federal portal counts for Bauchi record 1,932,456 learners and 21,227 classrooms, which yield approximately 91 learners per classroom if simply divided. The same portal displays a learner-to-classroom ratio of 66.6. Different school levels, definitions, ownership filters or room types may explain the mismatch; no alternative ratio should be substituted until the calculation rule and data extract are obtained. The fact that a simple arithmetic cross-check does not match is a legitimate request for metadata, not evidence that the underlying system is fraudulent. [E01])
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 681 0 R
/T (Functionality varies over time. A toilet marked 'present' may not operate, a borehole may be dry during certain seasons, an electricity connection may fail regularly, and a building may contain classrooms not fit for use. A robust school audit must therefore inspect actual service at a documented moment, record last maintenance, assign a person responsible and use repeat observations where seasonality matters. For every rehabilitation programme the data chain should include site ID, diagnosis, scope, awarded contract, physical verification, operation, handover, maintenance budget and post-handover condition. [E19, E06])
/E (Functionality varies over time. A toilet marked 'present' may not operate, a borehole may be dry during certain seasons, an electricity connection may fail regularly, and a building may contain classrooms not fit for use. A robust school audit must therefore inspect actual service at a documented moment, record last maintenance, assign a person responsible and use repeat observations where seasonality matters. For every rehabilitation programme the data chain should include site ID, diagnosis, scope, awarded contract, physical verification, operation, handover, maintenance budget and post-handover condition. [E19, E06])
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
