/T (The inclusion dimension cannot be reduced to a disability count. Learners with physical, sensory, cognitive or psychosocial challenges may require changes in access, communications, learning materials and teacher support. Girls require safe and private sanitation and clear safeguarding processes. Remoteness may raise transport and emergency risks for all children. Context-specific hazard mapping, school WASH and accessibility protocols should be undertaken alongside the teacher and enrolment audits, rather than as separate and potentially duplicative exercises.)
