/T (The AGILE programme provides a potentially useful implementation platform. Programme communications in February 2026 reported 12,133 conditional cash-transfer beneficiaries in 100 secondary schools, alongside support for school renovation, life skills and community engagement. Those figures are an output baseline requiring routine verification. A robust evaluation would examine eligible girls and selection rules, approved and successful payments, beneficiary receipt, grievances, attendance persistence, grade transition, completion, wellbeing and learning. It should also account for girls who are eligible but not selected and for differences across schools. The size of a programme's reach is not a direct measure of additional enrolment attributable to the intervention. [E03, E04])
/E (The AGILE programme provides a potentially useful implementation platform. Programme communications in February 2026 reported 12,133 conditional cash-transfer beneficiaries in 100 secondary schools, alongside support for school renovation, life skills and community engagement. Those figures are an output baseline requiring routine verification. A robust evaluation would examine eligible girls and selection rules, approved and successful payments, beneficiary receipt, grievances, attendance persistence, grade transition, completion, wellbeing and learning. It should also account for girls who are eligible but not selected and for differences across schools. The size of a programme's reach is not a direct measure of additional enrolment attributable to the intervention. [E03, E04])
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
