/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 684 0 R
/T (Earlier GEP3 experience in northern Nigeria, including Bauchi, offers reasons for cautious optimism about combined financial and community support, but its frequently quoted enrolment gains refer to a multi-state programme rather than a Bauchi-specific causal estimate. Comparative randomised research on cash transfers for schooling in Malawi also reveals important design choices: conditions can influence attendance during a programme, while other welfare outcomes may differ. Bauchi should therefore evaluate retention, wellbeing and safety together, not simply report the number of transfers issued. [E14, E15, E16, E17, E18])
/E (Earlier GEP3 experience in northern Nigeria, including Bauchi, offers reasons for cautious optimism about combined financial and community support, but its frequently quoted enrolment gains refer to a multi-state programme rather than a Bauchi-specific causal estimate. Comparative randomised research on cash transfers for schooling in Malawi also reveals important design choices: conditions can influence attendance during a programme, while other welfare outcomes may differ. Bauchi should therefore evaluate retention, wellbeing and safety together, not simply report the number of transfers issued. [E14, E15, E16, E17, E18])
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [4]
