/T (The Dogar, Shakeel and Tooley 2025 research provides a useful demonstration of the measurement issue, reporting a large share of sampled children engaged in some form of learning in Bauchi. That study was based on different provider and attendance definitions from MICS, and sampling limitations constrain statewide interpretation. The existence of educational activity outside the formal registry must not be mistaken for attainment of national minimum competencies. Conversely, classifying every child outside the formal register as receiving no educational experience can obscure opportunities for co-designed integration and quality assurance. [E29])
