/T (Historic Almajiri model-school experience offers a warning about building without institutional continuity. A new school may exist physically but have no recurrent staffing model, maintenance, sustained learner demand or accepted governance. Any integration proposal should therefore require formal agreements with credible local providers and families, appropriate curriculum and language design, qualified instructional support, a named safeguarding lead, financing beyond capital construction and independent evidence of competency progression. [E03, E04, E14, E15, E16, E17, E18])
