/T (Recognition and integration should be framed as an educational quality partnership, rather than simply enforcement or replacement. The state might offer teacher coaching, curriculum bridges, access to textbooks, assessment and transitions into recognised qualifications. Its design must be negotiated with the affected communities, respect applicable laws and learner rights, and test a small number of options before scaling. The potential benefit is substantial, but the current evidence does not establish which pathway design will prove acceptable, affordable or effective in Bauchi.)
