/T (Bauchi already has several instruments capable of supporting education reform: the national compulsory-basiceducation framework, state education authorities, SUBEB and LGEAs, annual basic-education planning mechanisms, curriculum and assessment systems, gender and school re-entry policy commitments, AGILE implementation and potentially expanded HOPE-EDU participation. This institutional presence is an asset. The challenge is to determine whether responsibilities are unambiguous, plans align with actual school deficits, financing reaches implementers and outcome evidence informs decisions. [E26, E08, E09, E28])
/E (Bauchi already has several instruments capable of supporting education reform: the national compulsory-basiceducation framework, state education authorities, SUBEB and LGEAs, annual basic-education planning mechanisms, curriculum and assessment systems, gender and school re-entry policy commitments, AGILE implementation and potentially expanded HOPE-EDU participation. This institutional presence is an asset. The challenge is to determine whether responsibilities are unambiguous, plans align with actual school deficits, financing reaches implementers and outcome evidence informs decisions. [E26, E08, E09, E28])
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [1]
>>
