/T (The institutional system is best analysed through decision rights. The Ministry should be able to define standards, policy priorities and review mechanisms within its lawful mandate; SUBEB should maintain a certified basiceducation school and teacher register and connect support to learning needs; LGEAs should act on local school conditions and attendance; finance and budget institutions should reconcile expenditure; and programme units should report externally funded results in interoperable formats. Where authority lies with federal agencies, The relevant authorities should not invent powers for the state. The first technical task is to confirm current statutory mandates and operating agreements, rather than prescribe a new committee by default.)
/E (The institutional system is best analysed through decision rights. The Ministry should be able to define standards, policy priorities and review mechanisms within its lawful mandate; SUBEB should maintain a certified basiceducation school and teacher register and connect support to learning needs; LGEAs should act on local school conditions and attendance; finance and budget institutions should reconcile expenditure; and programme units should report externally funded results in interoperable formats. Where authority lies with federal agencies, The relevant authorities should not invent powers for the state. The first technical task is to confirm current statutory mandates and operating agreements, rather than prescribe a new committee by default.)
