/T (The education system has also begun to invest in data infrastructure. The federal DNEMIS portal and state EMIS functions create an opportunity for school-level planning. Yet public inconsistencies between federal and state totals, within some state web tables, and between certain federal counts and ratios demonstrate the need for routine metadata, versioning and published correction protocols. Transparency is strengthened when data custodians explain differences rather than when researchers simply select the values supporting an argument.)
