/T (India offers both encouraging and cautionary examples. An experimental evaluation of monitored teacher attendance in a narrow non-formal school setting reported lower absence and higher test scores. The mechanism shows that verified implementation matters, but its camera-based incentive model cannot simply be imposed on civil-service schools without legal, labour, privacy and feasibility analysis. Separate experiments found that providing local committees with information about school oversight did not automatically improve teacher effort or pupil learning. For Bauchi, this means committees need authority, usable feedback and an actual issue-resolution route; information leaflets alone are insufficient. [E14, E15, E16, E17, E18])
/E (India offers both encouraging and cautionary examples. An experimental evaluation of monitored teacher attendance in a narrow non-formal school setting reported lower absence and higher test scores. The mechanism shows that verified implementation matters, but its camera-based incentive model cannot simply be imposed on civil-service schools without legal, labour, privacy and feasibility analysis. Separate experiments found that providing local committees with information about school oversight did not automatically improve teacher effort or pupil learning. For Bauchi, this means committees need authority, usable feedback and an actual issue-resolution route; information leaflets alone are insufficient. [E14, E15, E16, E17, E18])
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [5]
>>
