/T (The transferable principle is the combination of practical teaching support and implementation discipline. Books that arrive without teacher guides and lesson use may have limited effect; training without coaching may decay; coaching without assessment data may be unfocused. A programme assessment in Bauchi should therefore review teaching-material quality and availability, observed lesson delivery, mentor caseload, travel feasibility and how often instructional problems are discussed and resolved.)
/E (The transferable principle is the combination of practical teaching support and implementation discipline. Books that arrive without teacher guides and lesson use may have limited effect; training without coaching may decay; coaching without assessment data may be unfocused. A programme assessment in Bauchi should therefore review teaching-material quality and availability, observed lesson delivery, mentor caseload, travel feasibility and how often instructional problems are discussed and resolved.)
