/T (Interventions should also be assessed as complements or alternatives. Improving school attendance without raising instruction quality may increase time spent in low-learning environments. Improving teacher presence without books, lesson support or evaluation may generate limited gains. Introducing a learning technology programme before electricity, maintenance or teacher readiness can create stranded assets. A sensible portfolio therefore focuses on small sets of compatible inputs linked to actual service and outcome indicators. [E14, E15, E16, E17, E18])
