/T (The strategic reform objective is to establish a small number of durable operating routines through which evidence is converted into education service decisions. First, every school and relevant learning provider should have a stable, documented identifier. Second, learning and attendance indicators should be updated by responsible institutions with reproducible definitions. Third, school and teacher needs should be assessed against standards and actively responded to. Fourth, state and externally supported education finance should be joinable to projects, operations and service outputs. Fifth, officials and communities should receive clear feedback and an agreed process for resolving problems.)
/E (The strategic reform objective is to establish a small number of durable operating routines through which evidence is converted into education service decisions. First, every school and relevant learning provider should have a stable, documented identifier. Second, learning and attendance indicators should be updated by responsible institutions with reproducible definitions. Third, school and teacher needs should be assessed against standards and actively responded to. Fourth, state and externally supported education finance should be joinable to projects, operations and service outputs. Fifth, officials and communities should receive clear feedback and an agreed process for resolving problems.)
/Pg 73 0 R
/K [1]
