/E (The Teacher Allocation and Instructional Support Protocol would use a certified school-level teacher roster, grade and subject needs, personnel identity and attendance verification, agreed transfer standards and practical coaching arrangements. Necessary changes to postings should account for fairness, legal constraints, safe accommodation and retention. The implementation should track not only new teachers appointed but also how staffing and lesson delivery change in the most underserved schools.)
