/T (The recommended Foundational Learning Delivery Compact would connect a grade-specific assessment, lesson support, teaching material sufficiency, teacher coaching and regular follow-up. It should begin in schools selected through a fair, transparent and verified needs assessment. Its central measures should be the number and proportion of pupils improving in comparable proficiency categories, actual instructional delivery, attendance and the programme's cost. No single project-brand score should substitute for independent learner measurements.)
/E (The recommended Foundational Learning Delivery Compact would connect a grade-specific assessment, lesson support, teaching material sufficiency, teacher coaching and regular follow-up. It should begin in schools selected through a fair, transparent and verified needs assessment. Its central measures should be the number and proportion of pupils improving in comparable proficiency categories, actual instructional delivery, attendance and the programme's cost. No single project-brand score should substitute for independent learner measurements.)
/Pg 74 0 R
/K [3]
