/T (The Minimum Functional School Standard would combine basic classrooms, WASH, safeguarding, usable teaching materials, accessibility and affordable maintenance. It should be paired with an issue-resolution system that records a problem, assigns institutional responsibility, specifies a deadline appropriate to its urgency and verifies completion. Priorities would be driven by measured service deficits rather than broad geographic formulas. Projects without a credible operations and maintenance arrangement should not be classified as service-ready.)
/E (The Minimum Functional School Standard would combine basic classrooms, WASH, safeguarding, usable teaching materials, accessibility and affordable maintenance. It should be paired with an issue-resolution system that records a problem, assigns institutional responsibility, specifies a deadline appropriate to its urgency and verifies completion. Priorities would be driven by measured service deficits rather than broad geographic formulas. Projects without a credible operations and maintenance arrangement should not be classified as service-ready.)
