/T (The monitoring system should adopt an explicit indicator dictionary: definition; numerator and denominator; reporting unit; reference population; educational stage; reporting frequency; disaggregation; owner; evidence source; verification method; data confidentiality requirement; historical series; and any comparability break. A teacher-to-learner ratio without an agreed teacher definition is a poor metric. Similarly, an out-of-school figure without a specified age range, school/provider definition and denominator cannot meaningfully be compared across years.)
/E (The monitoring system should adopt an explicit indicator dictionary: definition; numerator and denominator; reporting unit; reference population; educational stage; reporting frequency; disaggregation; owner; evidence source; verification method; data confidentiality requirement; historical series; and any comparability break. A teacher-to-learner ratio without an agreed teacher definition is a poor metric. Similarly, an out-of-school figure without a specified age range, school/provider definition and denominator cannot meaningfully be compared across years.)
/Pg 82 0 R
