/T (Fieldwork should focus on unresolved mechanisms. A carefully stratified set of school and household visits can test staffing presence, working WASH, instructional guides, actual attendance, non-formal pathways and schoolcommunity constraints. It should use a defensible sample size for any generalisable estimates and avoid presenting purposive hotspot visits as state-representative. Interviews with children, pregnant or married girls and other vulnerable learners require special safeguarding. Datasets should be de-identified for analysis and access-controlled in storage.)
/E (Fieldwork should focus on unresolved mechanisms. A carefully stratified set of school and household visits can test staffing presence, working WASH, instructional guides, actual attendance, non-formal pathways and schoolcommunity constraints. It should use a defensible sample size for any generalisable estimates and avoid presenting purposive hotspot visits as state-representative. Interviews with children, pregnant or married girls and other vulnerable learners require special safeguarding. Datasets should be de-identified for analysis and access-controlled in storage.)
