/T (The federal 2024/25 administrative portal records 123,113 learners for Tafawa Balewa, with 35.9 learners per recorded teacher, 52.0 per reported classroom and 282.4 per recorded toilet; female teachers account for 32.9% of reported teaching staff. These are administrative aggregates rather than audited measures of daily teacher presence, functional room capacity or safe access to sanitation. The published special-needs count \(845\) also requires documentation of the underlying definition, referral status and duplication rules. [E01] The overall ratio is less extreme than in the highest-pressure LGAs, but could conceal severe school-level imbalances within the same LGA. Reported toilet pressure suggests a facilities-verification priority; the condition and access rules for existing units need review. Female-teacher distribution should be disaggregated by school, qualification and grade before any causal argument concerning inclusion. Interpretive limitation and source requirements: school and teacher master lists with common IDs; public/private/IQS coverage by level; school geolocations; operational classrooms and WASH facilities; anonymised teacher qualification and presence verification; and a signed record of denominator reconciliation. Any LGA prioritisation should be reconsidered after those records are obtained. )
