/Title (The federal 2024/25 administrative portal records 80,744 learners for Warji, with 106.1 learners per recorded teacher, 118.2 per reported classroom and 388.2 per recorded toilet; female teachers account for 30.0% of reported teaching staff. These are administrative aggregates rather than audited measures of daily teacher presence, functional room capacity or safe access to sanitation. The published special-needs count \(843\) also requires documentation of the underlying definition, referral status and duplication rules. [E01] The unusually large learner-to-teacher ratio is an urgent reason to reconcile payroll, postings, school coverage and reported enrolment before recommending a specific recruitment total. Reported toilet pressure is especially high. An independent inspection should measure the number of usable, safe, accessible and sex-appropriate toilets rather than inventory count alone. Female-teacher distribution should be disaggregated by school, qualification and grade before any causal argument concerning inclusion. Interpretive limitation and source requirements: school and teacher master lists with common IDs; public/private/IQS coverage by level; school geolocations; operational classrooms and WASH facilities; anonymised teacher qualification and presence verification; and a signed record of denominator reconciliation. Any LGA prioritisation should be reconsidered after those records are obtained.)
/Dest [100 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4228 0 R
>>
endobj
