/Title (This report offers a consolidated, independent assessment of basic and secondary education in Bauchi State, Nigeria. It brings together household-survey evidence, national learning assessments, administrative school statistics, education financing records, programme documentation and comparative research to examine whether schooling is translating into learning, completion and equitable opportunity. The findings and policy options are intended for state institutions, legislators, education practitioners, researchers, development partners and the public.)
