/Title (The federal 2024/25 administrative portal records 189,639 learners for Toro, with 52.4 learners per recorded teacher, 57.0 per reported classroom and 233.0 per recorded toilet; female teachers account for 38.3% of reported teaching staff. These are administrative aggregates rather than audited measures of daily teacher presence, functional room capacity or safe access to sanitation. The published special-needs count \(1,361\) also requires documentation of the underlying definition, referral status and duplication rules. [E01] The overall ratio is less extreme than in the highest-pressure LGAs, but could conceal severe school-level imbalances within the same LGA. The sanitation ratio must still be interpreted alongside functional water, cleanliness, privacy and maintenance. Female-teacher distribution should be disaggregated by school, qualification and grade before any causal argument concerning inclusion. Interpretive limitation and source requirements: school and teacher master lists with common IDs; public/private/IQS coverage by level; school geolocations; operational classrooms and WASH facilities; anonymised teacher qualification and presence verification; and a signed record of denominator reconciliation. Any LGA prioritisation should be reconsidered after those records are obtained.)
/Dest [99 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4446 0 R
