/Title (Claims are separated by both source class and inferential reach. Sample survey results describe the sampled population and require correct statistical weights, instrument definitions and uncertainty measures. Administrative census returns describe participating reporting units and depend on completeness, database version and denominators. Budget reports describe authorised and recorded financial flows subject to classification. A programme announcement establishes reported activity or intention, but cannot prove effect. External research can establish mechanisms in the studied setting; generalisation to Bauchi requires institutional and cultural transferability tests. [E04, E01, E05, E03, E06])
