/Title (When evaluating interventions, the preferred counter factual is a credible comparison group exposed to similar underlying conditions. Where an experiment or naturally staggered rollout is unavailable, interrupted time series and matched comparison designs may be considered, but they need baseline comparability, plausible controls and pre-specified outcomes. Simple before-and-after movements in attendance or examination scores cannot reliably be attributed to one programme because enrolment campaigns, economic shocks, changes in reporting and other education programmes may occur simultaneously.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4602 0 R
/Prev 4607 0 R
/Next 4613 0 R
>>
