/Title (Recent official narratives are more encouraging, but not directly comparable. In February 2026, Bauchi SUBEB reported that an estimated out-of-school population had fallen from more than 1.7 million in 2019 to around 216,000 as at December 2025, citing large enrolment campaigns, local mobilisation and attendance monitoring. It also reported 284,000 enrolments in a recent campaign. These statements establish what the Board reported, not independently verified changes in attendance or proficiency. The numerator and denominator used in the 2019 and 2025 counts, the underlying enumeration, age definitions, treatment of non-formal provision and duplicate-removal procedures have not yet been supplied for this research. [E02])
