/Title (An education system does not produce learning merely by listing schools and classrooms. The relevant service question is whether a child can attend a safe, accessible learning environment in which qualified teaching occurs for the expected duration. That requires usable rooms, seating, learning materials, reliable water, functioning sanitation, hygiene supplies, inclusion supports, protective routines and an identified maintenance responsibility. The federal 2024/25 census reported 206.7 learners per toilet in Bauchi, considerably above the published national ratio of 65.9; this is a signal to inspect actual services, not a verified measurement of usable cubicles or accessibility. [E01])
/Dest [36 0 R /Fit]
