/Title (The strategic reform objective is to establish a small number of durable operating routines through which evidence is converted into education service decisions. First, every school and relevant learning provider should have a stable, documented identifier. Second, learning and attendance indicators should be updated by responsible institutions with reproducible definitions. Third, school and teacher needs should be assessed against standards and actively responded to. Fourth, state and externally supported education finance should be joinable to projects, operations and service outputs. Fifth, officials and communities should receive clear feedback and an agreed process for resolving problems.)
/Dest [74 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4884 0 R
/Next 4904 0 R
>>
endobj
4893 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Minimum Functional School Standard would combine basic classrooms, WASH, safeguarding, usable teaching materials, accessibility and affordable maintenance. It should be paired with an issue-resolution system that records a problem, assigns institutional responsibility, specifies a deadline appropriate to its urgency and verifies completion. Priorities would be driven by measured service deficits rather than broad geographic formulas. Projects without a credible operations and maintenance arrangement should not be classified as service-ready.)
/Dest [74 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4884 0 R
/Prev 4905 0 R
>>
