/Count -1
/Next 5051 0 R
>>
endobj
5060 0 obj
<<
/Title (Before SDCI recommends a reform for large-scale adoption, the responsible institution should document: the precise local bottleneck, quality of causal and implementation evidence elsewhere, differences in language and culture, statutory mandate, cost per beneficiary, recurrent financing, workforce capacity, implementation fidelity, safeguards and a measurable stop/scale threshold. When any essential condition is unknown, the appropriate output is a feasibility study or evaluated pilot, not a promise of results.)
/Dest [62 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5051 0 R
>>
endobj
5061 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [62 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5042 0 R
/Prev 5052 0 R
/Next 5062 0 R
>>
endobj
5062 0 obj
<<
/Title (Comparators must be scrutinised for unintended effects: targeting can exclude children whose needs are not measured; high-stakes tests can create incentives to teach narrowly or manipulate results; recruitment incentives can attract staff to easier-to-measure schools; and digital interventions can divert funding from books, repairs and ongoing teacher support. The comparative cases are evidence inputs to local option appraisal, not turnkey programmes.)
/Dest [62 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5042 0 R
/Prev 5061 0 R
/Next 5053 0 R
>>
endobj
